 # F4 Cleanup Pass — Changes Summary
 
+## SimData Wave 3 — the missiles fly on their own motor, aero, and WEZ data (SIMDATA-3-1)
+
+**The last data family in SimData.zip with a real FreeFalcon runtime
+reader is engine-agnostic now. sim/MISDATA (MISTYPES.LST + 28 .dat
+files) — each missile's input block (39 sequential fields from maxTof
+to the fifteen "me123" boost/terminal-guide gains), mach×alpha cx/cz
+grids, motor thrust-vs-time breakpoints, the alt×vel×aspect WEZ RMax
+table, and the key-value aux tail — parses through f4-convert
+(msl2json) into canonical JSON (f4.misdata v1) and loads through
+f4-data with the reference's exact lookup contracts implemented
+(MissileAeroData::cx_at/cz_at = aero.cpp:36-46's TwodInterp,
+MissileEngineData::thrust_at = engine.cpp:15-22's OnedInterp with the
+hard zero after burnout, MissileRangeData::range_at = missmain.cpp:
+836-841's ThreedInterp behind GetRMax). The real consumer: f4-weapons'
+MissileConfig::from_simdata() builds the 3-DOF flyout config from the
+dataset — launch/burnout weight from wm0/wp0 (readin.cpp:18-27
+MissileClass::ReadInput), burn time from the motor table, thrust as
+the impulse-equivalent constant, cd from the cx grid (the shipped
+files store cx NEGATIVE for drag — aero.cpp:53's xaero = cx·qsom
+decelerates +x), seeker cone from atamax ("# Field of View (deg)"),
+PN gain from mslGnav, self-destruct at maxTof — and the aim9l round
+actually flies and terminates on its own data. THREE shipped-data
+quirks are documented, not hidden: (1) MISTYPES.LST declares 26 but
+lists 28 stems — the reference loop is count-driven, so sa8.dat and
+sa15.dat are DEAD FILES (present, unreachable; the parser mirrors the
+count and warns); (2) every shipped .dat is the ORIGINAL 24-field 1998
+input layout — the FreeFalcon reader consumes 39 (fifteen me123
+guidance fields were added to the reader after the files were
+authored), so the reference SHIFTS 15 tokens and reads garbage aero
+counts (numAlpha goes negative on every file); the parser tries the
+39-field order first, validation fails, it falls back to the legacy
+24-field order with the guidance fields = 0.0 and a loud warning
+(MissileInputData::format records which); (3) 2_75In.dat's cx
+multiplier is 0.1 — the only non-unity table multiplier in the zip,
+folded into the stored values exactly as readin.cpp:235-244 does. The
+aux tail (ParseSimlibFile semantics: case-insensitive keys, unknown
+keys silently ignored — the port warns, hex ints, "x,y,z" vectors) is
+fully implemented even though no shipped file carries aux data: every
+.dat ends at the range table, so the aux values are exactly the
+reader's documented defaults. Suite 2054 -> 2092.**
+
